# When this file exists the Vercel CLI reads it INSTEAD of .gitignore,
# so the first block mirrors .gitignore exactly.
node_modules/
.next/
.next-geobuild/
out/
.DS_Store
*.log
.env
.env.local
.envrc
.vercel
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts
__pycache__/
*.pyc
experiments/cube3d/verify/shots/
data/geo/*.geojson
/shots/

# CLI-deploy extras: agent worktrees and session state live under .claude/
# (ignored only via .git/info/exclude, which the CLI does not read) — a
# worktree carrying its own node_modules is ~600MB and aborts the upload.
.claude/

# The Vercel build runs in web/ (Root Directory) and touches nothing else.
# data/ and design/ feed MANUAL scripts (npm run data / design:sync) whose
# outputs are committed under web/; experiments and prototypes are standalone.
# Excluding them turns a ~100MB upload that dies mid-flight into a ~10MB one.
#
# ANCHORED WITH A LEADING SLASH, and this is load-bearing: this file applies
# to GIT deployments too, not only CLI uploads, and gitignore syntax makes an
# unanchored `data/` match a directory named data at ANY depth — which
# stripped web/src/data/ (the app's entire corpus) out of the deployment and
# failed the production build in nine seconds. Root-level only, by name.
/data/
/design/
/experiments/
/prototypes/
/review.html
/BACKLOG.md
